  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nSub-PR 1 of 2 for #4176 (K2, the guide stage). This PR adds the ring and the row guide planners: the two families that 2D Pocket needs. Part 2 (the medial line, the trace of a chain and the helix) follows on the same issue.\n\n## What changed\n\nPublic surface in `camcraft_pathkernel::guide`:\n- `RingPlanner`: rings as level sets of the distance to the walls (Held 1991), spaced by the stepover of the choice. `RingRef::Boundary` uses all edges. `RingRef::Part` uses the part walls only; its rings are open at the stock edge.\n- Clean-up rings fill the area that the regular rings leave. The 0.1 mm2 guard makes the result `Incomplete` with each gap named.\n- `RowPlanner`: rows at the angle, spaced evenly at the stepover or less, clipped to the cutter-centre area. A closing ring is added on request.\n- `Guides`: sends rings and rows to their planners. It refuses the medial line and the trace with `FAMILY_NOT_YET` until part 2 (law 4).\n- `Mark`, `MarkKind` (`FullWidth`, `Fill`, `Closing`; `#[non_exhaustive]`), `Span`. `GuideSet::with_marks` and `GuideSet::marks`. `GuideSet::new` does not change.\n- `FullWidth` names each stretch where the tool disc overlaps no disc of the next deeper curves and no air (#3788). K3 and K4 read it.\n- Named refusals: `NOT_RINGS`, `NOT_ROWS`, `CIRCLE_NOT_YET`, `BAND_NOT_YET`, `OFFSET_BELOW_CENTER`, `WALL_STRIP_UNCUT`, `NO_RING`, `TOO_MANY_RINGS`, `TOO_MANY_ROWS`, `STEP_ABOVE_DIAMETER`, `BAD_TOL`, `NOT_PLANAR`, `GUIDE_GEOMETRY`, `BAD_STRETCH`, `MARK_NO_CURVE`, `MARK_OFF_CURVE`.\n\nThe kernel crate still depends on `camcraft-geometry` only. No geometry function was added. No old planner and no golden changes: with the default switch the output is identical.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/guide_rings.rs` (11 tests): level-set spacing, law 1 under a permuted selection, Part equal to Boundary without a stock edge, the waist (two lobes, a neck narrower than two steps: the full-width stretch of each strand is named), clean-up rings, a small piece kept (0.01 mm2), a ring count, rings round a part, each refusal, `Guides`.\n- `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/guide_rows.rs` (6 tests): row spacing, rows at an angle with a closing ring, gaps named without a closing ring, law 1, refusals, mark checks. Helpers in `guide_kit.rs`.\n- `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_levels/kernel_rings.rs`: the kernel rings against the recorded old rings (#3750 goldens). Readings (agreement within 0.02 mm):\n  - Dog bone, 2D Offset round the part: each point of the 29 kernel rings is on each of the 7 old plans with a known stock. Named difference: the old plan also walks the stock outline; the kernel does not, because the outline is air (#4025 decision 4).\n  - `auto_blind` is not compared: an Outside kernel region needs the stock.\n  - The band round the disc: the 2D Pocket rings and the 3-D level rings are the old Auto rings, both ways. Named difference: the old Inside and Outside plans build their own pieces for each start side (#3316, #3750).\n- Law suite registry: this PR adds no registry row. When 2D Pocket moves, its row in `tests/laws/registry.rs` becomes `State::Moved` with `Planners { guide: Box::new(Guides), .. }`.\n\n## Gates on the final head `74766eaa5` (base `origin/side/path-kernel`)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel`: green (pathkernel lib, pathkernel laws, motion pass_start_levels).\n- The whole pathkernel `laws` suite: 98 passed (the guard grids included).\n- Motion `kernel_rings` and `kernel_baseline` pins: 17 passed.\n- `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`: green.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: green, 7 of 7 steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-pathkernel -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Review fixes (review of head 8977cd5f0)\n\n- Finding 1 (the guard area was narrowed by the first offset): commit f54a11059. One guard for both planners reads the whole centre area. `WALL_STRIP_UNCUT` refuses a clearing ring choice with a first offset above the tool radius. A ring count names the uncut area in a note.\n- Findings 2 to 4 (a dropped mark, the closing ring round an island, a full-width stretch on an open ring): commit 74766eaa5.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/4176-kernel-guides-rings-rows.md`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No planner calls the new code yet (no recipe on the kernel). The fig8 outline is not compared in this PR.\n- Exact circle rings and the band reference are refused by name: they come with the helix guide (part 2) and K4.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #4176\n",
